  "criterion": "Written before the Ticket 10 evidence runs (after a disclosed CPU pilot; docs/l2l/10_merge.md). Case merge_equivalence: export.merge.stream_merge merges the adapter into the base checkpoint tensor by tensor on the CPU (a child process that never initializes CUDA); the merged checkpoint, loaded on its own as a plain Hugging Face model, and the adapter-attached model run through the L2L engine on identical validation prompts. SUPPORTED iff for every variant (tiny fp32, tiny bf16; the real Qwen3-0.6B bf16 with the runs/qwen step-90 adapter) every merged tensor is one correct rounding of W0 + (alpha/r) B A (within half an ulp element by element; tolerances.yaml merge_equivalence), merged logits agree with the adapter-attached model's within the dtype's bound (fp32 1e-4, bf16 2^-4 of the largest logit), greedy tokens agree except at near-ties, the adapter's own effect is at least 100 (fp32) / 10 (bf16) times the merge discrepancy, every adapted tensor changed, the merged checkpoint loads independently with its tied embedding / head and no LoRA tensors, and on a GPU the merged evaluation's peak allocated memory stays below the model's size.",
